 "title": "Inner product and projections",
 "short": "Inner product and projections",
 "lead": "The <span data-concept=\"dot-product\">dot product</span>, written as the <span data-concept=\"inner-product\">inner product</span>, measures lengths and angles in any number of dimensions. This section uses it to say when two vectors are <span data-concept=\"orthogonal-vectors\">orthogonal</span>, to project one vector onto another as its shadow, and to build <span data-concept=\"orthogonal-basis\">orthogonal bases</span> by the <span data-concept=\"gram-schmidt-process\">Gram–Schmidt process</span>, the idea Chapter 4 carries over to functions.",
