   "cite": "orthogonal",
   "prompt": "<p>Find the $s$ that makes the following vectors orthogonal: $(1,2,3)$, $(1,1,s)$.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "number",
    "value": -1,
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "solution": "Two vectors are orthogonal when their inner product is zero. Here $\\langle (1,2,3), (1,1,s) \\rangle = 1 \\cdot 1 + 2 \\cdot 1 + 3s = 3 + 3s$, which is $0$ exactly when $s = -1$."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "e2",
   "source_id": "A.5.2",
   "source_number": "A.5.2",
   "kind": "exercise",
   "bloom": "Apply",
