   },
   "cite": "cos-intro",
   "prompt": "<p>Find the angle $\\ktheta$ between $(1,3,1)$, $(2,1,-1)$.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "number",
    "value": 1.056,
    "tol": 0.001,
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "solution": "$\\cos \\ktheta = \\frac{\\langle (1,3,1), (2,1,-1) \\rangle}{\\lVert (1,3,1) \\rVert \\lVert (2,1,-1) \\rVert} = \\frac{2 + 3 - 1}{\\sqrt{11}\\,\\sqrt{6}} = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{66}} \\approx 0.4924$, so with $0 \\leq \\ktheta \\leq \\pi$, $\\ktheta = \\cos^{-1}\\bigl(4/\\sqrt{66}\\bigr) \\approx 1.0560$ (radians)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "e3",
   "source_id": "A.5.3",
   "source_number": "A.5.3",
   "kind": "exercise",
   "bloom": "Apply",
   "place": {
