   },
   "cite": "projection-def",
   "prompt": "<p>Suppose $\\kvecv = (1,1,-1)$. Find</p><ol type=\"a\"><li>$\\kproj_{\\kvecv}\\bigl( (1,0,0) \\bigr)$</li><li>$\\kproj_{\\kvecv}\\bigl( (1,2,3) \\bigr)$</li><li>$\\kproj_{\\kvecv}\\bigl( (1,-1,0) \\bigr)$</li></ol>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "solution": "Here $\\langle \\kvecv , \\kvecv \\rangle = 1 + 1 + 1 = 3$. a) $\\langle (1,0,0), \\kvecv \\rangle = 1$, so $\\kproj_{\\kvecv}\\bigl((1,0,0)\\bigr) = \\frac{1}{3}(1,1,-1) = \\left(\\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{1}{3}, \\frac{-1}{3}\\right)$. b) $\\langle (1,2,3), \\kvecv \\rangle = 1 + 2 - 3 = 0$, so the projection is $\\vec{0} = (0,0,0)$: $(1,2,3)$ is orthogonal to $\\kvecv$. c) $\\langle (1,-1,0), \\kvecv \\rangle = 1 - 1 + 0 = 0$, so again the projection is $(0,0,0)$."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "e5",
   "source_id": "A.5.5",
