   "cite": "gram-schmidt-start",
   "prompt": "<p>Let $\\kS$ be the subspace spanned by $(1,3,-1)$, $(1,1,1)$. Find an orthogonal basis of $\\kS$ by the Gram–Schmidt process.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "open",
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "solution": "$\\kvecw_1 = (1,3,-1)$. Then $\\langle (1,1,1), \\kvecw_1 \\rangle = 1 + 3 - 1 = 3$ and $\\langle \\kvecw_1, \\kvecw_1 \\rangle = 11$, so $\\kvecw_2 = (1,1,1) - \\frac{3}{11}(1,3,-1) = \\left(\\frac{8}{11}, \\frac{2}{11}, \\frac{14}{11}\\right)$. The orthogonal basis is $(1,3,-1)$, $\\left(\\frac{8}{11}, \\frac{2}{11}, \\frac{14}{11}\\right)$ (or $(4,1,7)$ after scaling by $\\frac{11}{2}$); check: $\\frac{8}{11} + \\frac{6}{11} - \\frac{14}{11} = 0$."
   }
  },
